    body: 'Xenon reads FPS in games with PresentMon. Since 5.1.0 Xenon never runs as administrator on Windows, so PresentMon needs the Windows group Performance Log Users: the "Enable sensors" confirmation adds the user to it. Windows applies a group only from the next sign-in, so when FPS stopped showing after updating to 5.1.0, or right after enabling the sensors, the fix is to sign out of Windows and back in, or restart the PC; restarting Xenon alone is not enough. Xenon tells which case it is while a game runs: the Game performance tile and Settings → Performance → "FPS in games" say "sign out and back in" when the permission is granted but not yet active, and offer an "Allow FPS" button (one Windows confirmation) when it is missing. A pop-up at the top says it too, once per Xenon version, the first time a game runs without FPS. If FPS is still missing after signing in again, the game may block frame readers (some anti-cheat do). macOS and Linux are not affected by this permission.',
