    body: 'Someone who writes widget code in Claude Code, Codex or any MCP client can connect it to Xenon: Xenon → Create and share → "Build widgets with Claude Code or Codex" has a Connect button for each (it adds the xenon-widgets MCP server to that program), or by hand `claude mcp add --scope user xenon-widgets -- npx -y xenon-mcp` / `codex mcp add xenon-widgets -- npx -y xenon-mcp`; Claude Code can also install the xenon-widgets plugin, which adds a build-widget skill. The first time the assistant uses it, the dashboard asks "Let this tool build widgets?"; connected tools are listed in that same card with a Remove button. The assistant can then read the Widget SDK, write a starter widget in a folder, check it, install it and put it on the page, read the errors and blocked requests it hits while running, and take a picture of its tile, then fix it. It never approves a widget\'s permissions (the person still does, on the dashboard), can only change the person\'s own widgets, and works only from this PC, never from a paired phone. Thrown errors in widget code show as "Script error." because of the sandbox; console.error messages arrive in full. Screenshots do not work on Linux under Wayland. Bit itself can also make a widget from a sentence; the MCP is for people who want to write the code with their own assistant.',
