    body: 'Sparks are Xenon\'s credits; always use the app\'s name for them in the user\'s language (Scintille, Chispas, Étincelles, Funken, Faíscas, Искры, Vonken, スパーク, 스파크, 火花), never "credits" alone. The provider Bit (Settings → Bit) runs on them, no API key. Supporters get 300 Sparks each calendar month, spent first; unused ones do not carry over. Under 5 USD is a tip: no access, no Sparks. Anyone can buy packs in the Store, under Sparks (500 Sparks for 5 USD, 1,050 for 10 USD, 2,200 for 20 USD); bought Sparks never expire and also buy Store items. They arrive within a minute, at most a day; with no code saved, or paying with another email, an XC code comes by email, to paste in Settings under Supporter code; pasted beside a pass, its Sparks and later packs from that email join it. Questions, commands and voice always run on Haiku, for less than one Spark an answer. For creations the user picks the model: Haiku (a widget costs about 3 Sparks), Sonnet (balanced, about 80) or Opus (the most accurate, about 150), at the Normal level. The app calls them Fast, Smart and Smartest (Veloce, Bravo, Il più bravo): use those names. Reasoning sets how much the model thinks: Light suits simple requests (Sparks close to Normal), Normal is the recommended balance, Thorough gives a more polished result for about twice the Sparks and the time. The assistant changes both when asked ("use the smartest", "think more") with set_creation_model, effective at once. The creation arrives at every level. The balance shows in Settings, in the Store and at the top of the chat; a tap opens the model panel.',
